{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-23799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d6010443fab46eee3cb4ab3cf76eab2466efba1a76cea7725235c40135f67f5"} {"question" "q-23799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta $ using its definition and simplify further:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d6010443fab46eee3cb4ab3cf76eab2466efba1a76cea7725235c40135f67f5"} {"question" "q-23799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "789647efc47e67cffb1b5477a7d074db79cdbe37071cba63283bf1370f324314"} {"question" "q-23799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d6010443fab46eee3cb4ab3cf76eab2466efba1a76cea7725235c40135f67f5"} {"question" "q-23799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d6010443fab46eee3cb4ab3cf76eab2466efba1a76cea7725235c40135f67f5"} {"question" "q-23799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d6010443fab46eee3cb4ab3cf76eab2466efba1a76cea7725235c40135f67f5"} {"question" "q-65230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression $\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d6010443fab46eee3cb4ab3cf76eab2466efba1a76cea7725235c40135f67f5"} {"question" "q-65230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}=\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the numerator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1} & =\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d6010443fab46eee3cb4ab3cf76eab2466efba1a76cea7725235c40135f67f5"} {"question" "q-65230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972325/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "789647efc47e67cffb1b5477a7d074db79cdbe37071cba63283bf1370f324314"} {"question" "q-65230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacad